ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE RESEARCH INDUSTRY PROMOTION ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Research Industry Promotion Act and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Scope of Research Industry)
The scope of each detailed sector of the research industry shall be as specified in attached Table 1.

Article 3 (Formulation of Master Plans and Implementation Plans for Promotion of Research Industry)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT formulates a master plan for the promotion of the research industry under Article 4 (1) of the Research Industry Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") (hereinafter referred to as a "master plan") and an implementation plan for the promotion of the research industry under paragraph (3) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan"), the Minister shall undergo deliberation by the National Science and Technology Advisory Council under the National Science and Technology Advisory Council Act. The same shall apply to amendments to a master plan or implementation plan.
(2) Where necessary for formulating and implementing master plans and implementation plans, the Minister of Science and ICT may request the heads of relevant central administrative agencies or local governments to submit materials.
(3) Where the Minister of Science and ICT formulates or amends a master plan and an implementation plan pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall publicly announce them in the Official Gazette or on the website of the Ministry of Science and ICT.

Article 4 (Compilation of Statistics and Fact-Finding Surveys on Research Industry)
(1) Statistics on the research industry under Article 5 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "research industry statistics") shall include the following matters:
1. The status of domestic and overseas markets for the research industry;
2. Matters concerning the status of personnel in the research industry and the actual conditions of their supply and demand;
3. Matters concerning the sales and actual management conditions of research business operators and specialized research business operators;
4. The status of research and development related to the research industry;
5. Other matters necessary for formulating and implementing policies to promote the research industry.
(2) The Minister of Science and ICT shall compile research industry statistics once each year and may compile them from time to time where necessary.
(3) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to conduct a fact-finding survey under Article 5 (2) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "fact-finding survey"), the Minister shall formulate a survey plan including the date and time, subjects, purpose, and content of the fact-finding survey, and shall notify the subjects of the survey of the plan in advance.
(4) Fact-finding surveys shall be conducted by means of field surveys, questionnaire surveys, literature surveys, or similar methods, and may be conducted using information and communications networks, such as electronic mail, where necessary for efficient surveys.

Article 5 (Requirements for Reporting as Specialized Research Business Operators)
(1) "Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as specialized personnel" in Article 6 (1) of the Act means the requirements according to the following classifications:
1. A person engaging in the research industry referred to in subparagraph 1 (a) of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "contract research industry"): All of the following requirements:
(a) The person shall maintain at all times at least three personnel falling under either of the following and exclusively responsible for work concerning the contract research industry (excluding the representative; provided, the representative of a small enterprise under Article 2 (2) of the Framework Act on Small and Medium Enterprises for which three years have not elapsed since its establishment shall be included):
1) A person holding an associate degree or higher in the natural sciences, engineering, or medicine fields under attached Table 1 of the Regulations on the Establishment and Operation of Universities and Colleges (including a person recognized under statutes or regulations as having an equivalent or higher level of education);
2) A person who has obtained a qualification as a professional engineer, master craftsman, engineer, or industrial engineer in the technical and skills fields under subparagraph 1 of Article 9 of the National Technical Qualifications Act;
(b) The person shall have space dedicated to research that is separate from other workspaces (excluding space in an unauthorized building, a temporary building, or a house referred to in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Housing Act) and research equipment and materials used directly for research and development;
(c) Sales generated by the contract research industry shall account for at least 30 percent of the research business operator's total sales.
2. A person engaging in the research industry referred to in subparagraph 1 (b) of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "research management industry"): All of the following requirements:
(a) The person shall maintain at all times at least two personnel falling under either of the following and exclusively responsible for work concerning the research management industry (excluding the representative; provided, the representative of a small enterprise under Article 2 (2) of the Framework Act on Small and Medium Enterprises for which three years have not elapsed since its establishment shall be included):
1) A person falling under subparagraph 1 (a) 1) or 2);
2) A person holding an associate degree or higher in a field related to the relevant research management industry (including a person recognized under statutes or regulations as having an equivalent or higher level of education);
(b) Sales generated by the research management industry shall account for at least 30 percent of the research business operator's total sales.
3. A person engaging in the research industry referred to in subparagraph 1 (c) of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "research equipment industry"): All of the following requirements:
(a) The person shall maintain at all times at least two personnel falling under subparagraph 1 (a) 1) or 2) and exclusively responsible for work concerning the research equipment industry (excluding the representative; provided, the representative of a small enterprise under Article 2 (2) of the Framework Act on Small and Medium Enterprises for which three years have not elapsed since its establishment shall be included);
(b) The research business operator shall have developed at least one item of equipment, a peripheral system, or a component used for research and development;
(c) The person shall have a record of at least three deliveries per year of the equipment, peripheral systems, or components referred to in item (b).
4. A person engaging in the research industry referred to in subparagraph 1 (d) of Article 2 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "research materials industry"): All of the following requirements:
(a) The person shall maintain at all times at least two personnel falling under subparagraph 1 (a) 1) or 2) and exclusively responsible for work concerning the research materials industry (excluding the representative; provided, the representative of a small enterprise under Article 2 (2) of the Framework Act on Small and Medium Enterprises for which three years have not elapsed since its establishment shall be included);
(b) The research business operator shall have developed at least one material or substance necessary for research and development;
(c) The person shall have a record of at least three deliveries per year of the materials or substances referred to in item (b).
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), for the following sectors among the detailed sectors of the research industry specified in attached Table 1, the reporting requirements under Article 6 (1) of the Act shall be according to the following classifications:
1. Testing, inspection, and analysis within the contract research industry: All of the following requirements:
(a) At least two personnel under paragraph (1) 1 (a) shall be maintained at all times;
(b) The requirement referred to in paragraph (1) 1 (b);
(c) The requirement referred to in paragraph (1) 1 (c).
2. Maintenance and repair of research equipment within the research equipment industry: All of the following requirements:
(a) The requirement referred to in paragraph (1) 3 (a);
(b) A record of at least three instances of research equipment maintenance or repair per year.
(3) Notwithstanding paragraphs (1) and (2), where a person intending to report as a specialized research business operator pursuant to Article 6 (1) of the Act is a research business operator for which less than one year has elapsed since its establishment as of the reporting date (hereinafter referred to as a "new research business operator") and does not satisfy the sales requirements referred to in paragraph (1) 1 (c) or 2 (b) or paragraph (2) 1 (c), the development and delivery performance requirements referred to in paragraph (1) 3 (b) and (c) or 4 (b) and (c), or the maintenance and repair performance requirement referred to in paragraph (2) 2 (b) (hereinafter referred to in this paragraph as "sales and other performance requirements"), the sales and other performance requirements for the new research business operator shall be according to the following classifications. In such cases, the new research business operator shall satisfy the sales and other performance requirements by the time the report is renewed pursuant to Article 6 (5) of the Act.
1. The contract research industry or research management industry: The operator shall substantiate prospective sales by means of contracts or similar documents;
2. The research equipment industry (excluding research equipment maintenance and repair) or research materials industry: The operator shall substantiate that development is underway and substantiate prospective delivery performance by means of contracts or similar documents;
3. Research equipment maintenance and repair within the research equipment industry: The operator shall substantiate prospective maintenance and repair performance by means of contracts or similar documents.

Article 6 (Procedures for Reporting as Specialized Research Business Operators)
(1) A research business operator intending to file a report under Article 6 (1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Science and ICT a reporting form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT, together with documents substantiating that the requirements under Article 5 are satisfied.
(2) Upon receiving a reporting form under paragraph (1), the Minister of Science and ICT shall verify the certificate of business registration (meaning a certificate of business registration excluding the resident registration number; hereinafter the same shall apply) or certificate of registered corporate matters through joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act; provided, where the reporting person does not consent to verification of the certificate of business registration, the Minister shall require the person to attach the relevant document. <Amended on Apr. 23, 2024>
(3) Details concerning reporting as a specialized research business operator, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 7 (Supplementation of Reports)
(1) Where supplementation is necessary in a reporting form or accompanying documents submitted by a research business operator pursuant to Article 6 (1), the Minister of Science and ICT may require supplementation by setting a reasonable period necessary for it.
(2) The period required for supplementation under paragraph (1) shall not be included in the period referred to in Article 6 (3) of the Act.
(3) Where a research business operator requested to supplement a report pursuant to paragraph (1) fails to do so within the period allowed, the Minister of Science and ICT may return the submitted reporting form.
(4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT accepts a report pursuant to Article 6 (3) of the Act, the Minister shall issue to the reporting person a certificate of reporting as a specialized research business operator prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT.

Article 8 (Reports on Changes)
(1) "Important matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 6 (2) of the Act means the following matters:
1. Trade name or name;
2. Corporate registration number or business registration number;
3. Location of the principal place of business;
4. Representative;
5. Reported business sector;
6. Other matters for which the Minister of Science and ICT deems a report on changes necessary for the management of specialized research business operators.
(2) Where a specialized research business operator changes any matter referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1), the operator shall submit to the Minister of Science and ICT, within 14 days from the date of the change, a reporting form for changes prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT, together with documents substantiating the change and the certificate of reporting as a specialized research business operator.
(3) Where the Minister of Science and ICT, upon receiving a reporting form for changes under paragraph (2), accepts the report on changes pursuant to Article 6 (3) of the Act, the Minister shall issue a new certificate of reporting as a specialized research business operator.
(4) Even where a specialized research business operator files a report on changes pursuant to paragraphs (1) through (3), the validity period of the existing report shall remain unchanged.

Article 9 (Renewal of Reports)
(1) A specialized research business operator intending to renew a report pursuant to Article 6 (5) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Science and ICT, during the period beginning three months and ending one month before the expiry date, a reporting form for renewal prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT, together with documents substantiating that the requirements under Article 5 are satisfied.
(2) The validity period of a renewal report under Article 6 (5) of the Act shall be three years from the day following the date on which the validity period of the existing report expires.

Article 10 (Procedures for Research Equipment Performance Evaluation)
(1) A research business operator intending to undergo a research equipment performance evaluation under Article 8 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "research equipment performance evaluation") shall apply, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT, to an evaluation institution designated by the Minister of Science and ICT pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article (hereinafter referred to as an "evaluation institution").
(2) An evaluation institution shall conduct research equipment performance evaluations as determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT.
(3) An evaluation institution that has conducted a research equipment performance evaluation shall issue a report on the results of the research equipment performance evaluation, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT.
(4) A report on the results of a research equipment performance evaluation under paragraph (3) shall include the following matters:
1. Procedures for conducting the research equipment performance evaluation;
2. Items of the research equipment performance evaluation;
3. Criteria for each item of the research equipment performance evaluation;
4. Conformity with respect to each item of the research equipment performance evaluation.

Article 11 (Designation of Evaluation Institutions)
(1) The Minister of Science and ICT may designate as an evaluation institution, pursuant to Article 8 (3) of the Act, any of the following institutions or organizations that satisfies the requirements prescribed in paragraph (2):
1. A government-funded research institution under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutions;
2. A specific research institution under Article 2 of the Specific Research Institutions Support Act;
3. A specialized production technology research institute under Article 42 (1) of the Industrial Technology Innovation Promotion Act;
4. Other institutions or organizations established pursuant to the Civil Act or other Acts which the Minister of Science and ICT recognizes as having expertise in research equipment performance evaluation.
(2) A person intending to be designated as an evaluation institution pursuant to Article 8 (3) of the Act shall satisfy all of the following requirements and shall apply to the Minister of Science and ICT by submitting an application for designation as a research equipment performance evaluation institution prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Science and ICT, together with documents substantiating satisfaction of the designation requirements:
1. An organization suitable for conducting research equipment performance evaluations;
2. At least five personnel falling under the following items in the organization referred to in subparagraph 1:
(a) A person who has obtained a doctoral degree in science or engineering;
(b) A person who has at least three years of research or practical experience after obtaining a master's degree in science or engineering;
3. Office and testing space for conducting research equipment performance evaluations;
4. Facilities and equipment for conducting research equipment performance evaluations;
5. Other requirements that the Minister of Science and ICT deems necessary for conducting research equipment performance evaluations.
(3) Upon receiving an application for designation under paragraph (2), the Minister of Science and ICT shall verify the certificate of business registration or certificate of registered corporate matters through joint use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act; provided, where the applicant does not consent to verification of the certificate of business registration, the Minister shall require the applicant to attach the relevant document. <Amended on Apr. 23, 2024>
(4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT designates an evaluation institution pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall publicly notify that fact.
(5) Details concerning procedures for designation of evaluation institutions and related matters, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (4), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 12 (Revocation of Designation of Evaluation Institutions)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to revoke the designation of an evaluation institution on the ground referred to in Article 8 (4) 2 of the Act, the Minister may require the evaluation institution to satisfy the designation requirements within a specified period not exceeding 30 days, and may revoke its designation if it fails to satisfy the designation requirements within that period.
(2) Where the Minister of Science and ICT revokes the designation of an evaluation institution pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall publicly notify that fact.
(3) Details concerning procedures for revocation of designation of evaluation institutions and related matters, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 13 (Designation of Research Industry Promotion Complexes)
(1) The Minister of Science and ICT may designate an area satisfying all of the following requirements as a research industry promotion complex under Article 9 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "research industry promotion complex"):
1. Research business operators and specialized research business operators are concentrated in the area;
2. Universities, research institutes, and other institutions capable of supporting the growth of research business operators are located in the area;
3. There is sufficient demand for the research industry;
4. There is a high likelihood that the region's major industries and the research industry will develop in conjunction with each other;
5. The area will have substantial ripple effects on the research industry as a whole.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Minister of Science and ICT may designate as a research industry promotion complex an area which the Minister recognizes as having a high likelihood of a concentration of research business operators and their support facilities, etc. pursuant to Article 9 (1) of the Act for the promotion of the research industry, even if the area does not satisfy all of the requirements referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).
(3) A Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as a "Mayor/Do Governor") may apply to the Minister of Science and ICT for designation of an area under the Mayor/Do Governor's jurisdiction as a research industry promotion complex pursuant to paragraph (1) or (2).
(4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to designate a research industry promotion complex pursuant to paragraph (1) or (2), the Minister shall hear in advance the opinion of the Mayor/Do Governor having jurisdiction over the area intended for designation as a research industry promotion complex and may consult with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies where necessary.
(5) Where the Minister of Science and ICT designates a research industry promotion complex pursuant to paragraph (1) or (2), the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters:
1. The name, location, and area of the research industry promotion complex;
2. The purpose of designation of the research industry promotion complex;
3. The method of management of the research industry promotion complex.
(6) Details necessary for the designation and management of research industry promotion complexes and related matters, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (5), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 14 (Cancellation of Designation of Research Industry Promotion Complexes)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT intends to cancel the designation of a research industry promotion complex on any ground referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 9 (3) of the Act, the Minister shall hear in advance the opinion of the Mayor/Do Governor having jurisdiction over the research industry promotion complex and may consult with the heads of relevant central administrative agencies where necessary.
(2) Where the Minister of Science and ICT cancels the designation of a research industry promotion complex pursuant to paragraph (1), the Minister shall publicly notify the following matters and notify the competent Mayor/Do Governor and the heads of relevant central administrative agencies without delay:
1. The name and location of the research industry promotion complex whose designation is canceled;
2. The dates of designation and cancellation of designation of the research industry promotion complex;
3. The grounds for cancellation of designation of the research industry promotion complex.
(3) Matters necessary for cancellation of designation of research industry promotion complexes and related matters, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) and (2), shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Science and ICT.

Article 15 (Institutions Conducting Projects for International Cooperation and Promotion of Overseas Expansion)
"Institutions or organizations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (2) of the Act means the following institutions or organizations:
1. The research industry association under Article 13 of the Act;
2. An institution dedicated to the promotion of the research industry under Article 14 (1) of the Act;
3. Other institutions or organizations established pursuant to the Civil Act or other Acts which the Minister of Science and ICT recognizes as having expertise in conducting the projects referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 10 (1) of the Act.

Article 16 (Establishment and Operation of Research Industry Association)
(1) Research business operators intending to obtain authorization to establish a research industry association pursuant to Article 13 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "research industry association") shall submit the following documents to the Minister of Science and ICT:
1. Articles of association;
2. A list and curricula vitae of the promoters;
3. Letters of acceptance of appointment as officers;
4. A business plan and a budget revenue and expenditure plan;
5. Minutes of the inaugural meeting.
(2) The articles of association referred to in paragraph (1) 1 shall include the following matters:
1. Purpose and name;
2. Location of the principal office;
3. Matters concerning business;
4. Matters concerning membership qualifications;
5. Matters concerning officers.
(3) Where the research industry association intends to amend its articles of association, it shall resolve on the amendment at a general meeting and shall apply to the Minister of Science and ICT for authorization of the amendment within seven days from the date on which the general meeting ends.
(4) Where the Minister of Science and ICT authorizes the establishment of the research industry association pursuant to Article 13 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall publicly announce that fact in the Official Gazette or on the website of the Ministry of Science and ICT.
(5) The research industry association shall submit its business and budget plans for the relevant year and its performance for the preceding year to the Minister of Science and ICT by the end of March each year.

Article 17 (Functions of Research Industry Association)
The research industry association shall perform the following functions:
1. Making proposals for improvements to laws and systems concerning the research industry;
2. Functions concerning support for and fostering of research business operators;
3. Functions concerning the training of specialized personnel for the research industry;
4. Functions entrusted by the Minister of Science and ICT pursuant to Article 16 of the Act;
5. Other functions necessary for achieving the purposes of establishment of the research industry association.

Article 18 (Designation and Operation of Institutions Dedicated to Promotion of Research Industry)
(1) Where the Minister of Science and ICT designates an institution dedicated to the promotion of the research industry pursuant to Article 14 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "institution dedicated to research industry promotion") or revokes its designation pursuant to paragraph (3) of that Article, the Minister shall publicly notify that fact.
(2) An institution dedicated to research industry promotion shall submit its business and budget plans for the relevant year and its performance for the preceding year to the Minister of Science and ICT by the end of March each year.

Article 19 (Functions of Institutions Dedicated to Research Industry Promotion)
An institution dedicated to research industry promotion shall perform the following functions:
1. Supporting the formulation of policies for promotion of the research industry;
2. Creating an ecosystem and establishing foundations for promotion of the research industry;
3. Supporting research and development concerning the research industry;
4. Supporting industry-academia-research cooperation concerning the research industry;
5. Supporting publicity and events concerning the research industry;
6. Functions entrusted by the Minister of Science and ICT pursuant to Article 16 of the Act;
7. Other functions that the Minister of Science and ICT deems necessary for promotion of the research industry.

Article 20 (Requests for Reports and Submission of Documents)
Where the Minister of Science and ICT requests specialized research business operators, the research industry association, institutions dedicated to research industry promotion, etc. to make reports or submit relevant documents pursuant to Article 15 (1) of the Act, the Minister shall do so in writing clearly stating the purpose, scope, deadline, and other details of the request.

Article 21 (Entrustment of Functions)
(1) The Minister of Science and ICT may entrust the following functions to the institutions or organizations prescribed in paragraph (2) pursuant to Article 16 of the Act:
1. Compilation and management of research industry statistics;
2. Receipt and confirmation of reports, reports on changes, and renewal reports of specialized research business operators under Article 6 (1), (2), and (5) of the Act;
3. Surveys for the formulation and implementation of policy measures under Article 7 (2) of the Act;
4. Conducting projects referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 9 (2) of the Act;
5. Supporting projects referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 10 (1) of the Act;
6. Surveys and analysis under Article 11 (3) of the Act.
(2) Institutions or organizations to which functions may be entrusted pursuant to paragraph (1) shall be as follows:
1. The research industry association;
2. Institutions dedicated to research industry promotion;
3. Government-funded research institutions under the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutions;
4. Specific research institutions under Article 2 of the Specific Research Institutions Support Act;
5. Other institutions or organizations established pursuant to the Civil Act or other Acts which the Minister of Science and ICT recognizes as having expertise in the functions to be entrusted.
(3) Where the Minister of Science and ICT entrusts functions pursuant to paragraphs (1) and (2), the Minister shall publicly notify the entrusted institution or organization and the details of the entrusted functions.

Article 22 (Review of Regulation)
The Minister of Science and ICT shall examine the appropriateness of the requirements for reporting as a specialized research business operator under Article 5 every three years, based on January 1, 2022 (meaning before the day corresponding to the base date in every third year), and shall take measures such as making improvements.

Article 23 (Criteria for Imposition of Administrative Fines)
The criteria for imposing administrative fines under Article 18 (1) of the Act shall be as specified in attached Table 2.

